        {
            "number": 6,
            "revision": "4b35b8e3a41dd791e50dc56719a054623c127780",
            "parents": [
                "256dc5295117c96c96be48e8aef3e401e802262d"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/14/82114/6",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Zoey YJ Chung",
                "email": "zoey.yj.chung.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "zoeychung10"
            },
            "createdOn": 1753239682,
            "author": {
                "name": "Zoey YJ Chung",
                "email": "zoey.yj.chung.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "zoeychung10"
            },
            "kind": "NO_CODE_CHANGE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-yosemite4/recipes-phosphor/state/phosphor-state-manager/chassis-poweron@.service",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "These are not services that exist upstream.\n\nI don't understand why you're manually doing this though.  Those scripts can already specify their own Wants/After, right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-yosemite4/recipes-phosphor/state/phosphor-state-manager/chassis-poweron@.service",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Zoey YJ Chung",
                        "email": "zoey.yj.chung.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "zoeychung10"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks, I will fix this setting."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-yosemite4/recipes-phosphor/state/phosphor-state-manager/chassis-poweron@.service",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Zoey YJ Chung",
                        "email": "zoey.yj.chung.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "zoeychung10"
                    },
                    "message": "I tried setting in the scripts, but since the firmware version can only be triggered by ```WantedBy``` ```obmc-chassis-poweron target```, it causes ```obmc-chassis-poweron target``` process to take too long while waiting for the firmware version service to complete (synchronous waiting). Therefore, it moved the firmware version service to run after the ```chassis-poweron service```, so it won't affect the completion time of the ```obmc-chassis-poweron target``` process."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-yosemite4/recipes-phosphor/state/phosphor-state-manager/chassis-poweron@.service",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Zoey YJ Chung",
                        "email": "zoey.yj.chung.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "zoeychung10"
                    },
                    "message": "If the ```obmc-chassis-poweron target``` takes longer to active, it may cause the DC ON process to be delayed or mistakenly assume that AC ON has not been completed (since the DC-On target requires the AC-On target). As a result, it could cause AC ON to be triggered a second time."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-yosemite4/recipes-phosphor/state/phosphor-state-manager/policy-chassis-poweron",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Has anyone ever looked at all the `/run` tempfile stuff that phosphor-state-manager has?  Things like this are suppose to be ran as part of the pre-phosphor-discover-system-state code and it is suppose to set `/run` temporary files so phosphor-state-manager knows the system is already on (or off)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-yosemite4/recipes-phosphor/state/phosphor-state-manager/policy-chassis-poweron",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Zoey YJ Chung",
                        "email": "zoey.yj.chung.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "zoeychung10"
                    },
                    "message": "The reason for using \"obmc-chassis-poweron target is Active\" as a condition is due to the dependency that **DC-On target requires AC-On target** [setting](https://github.com/openbmc/openbmc/blob/master/meta-phosphor/recipes-phosphor/state/phosphor-state-manager_git.bb#L259C1-L261C93). For example, after running discover-system-state, if the system is in an ```alwaysOn``` state, it will trigger the DC-On target. This **ensures that the AC-On target is already active before executing the DC-On target**. If the AC-On target is not active, this may result in the AC-On sequence being triggered again. \n\nThis seems to be different from the intended use case of ```/run/openbmc/chassis@X-on```. The ```chassis@X-on``` file is removed once the obmc-chassis-poweron target becomes active. If I have misunderstood anything, please let me know. Thank you!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-yosemite4/recipes-phosphor/state/phosphor-state-manager/policy-chassis-poweron",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "The fact that we have to randomly run phosphor-discover-system-state is an indication to me that we're not using phosphor-state-manager correctly.  discover system state is intended to be ran when the BMC reboots to figure out the state of the server.\n\nHow does starting phosphor-discover-system-state relate to \"Power on Host\"??  This will only even do something if the host is already off and the policy is \"always on\".  If the policy is something else, this won't actually power on anything, right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-yosemite4/recipes-phosphor/state/phosphor-state-manager/policy-chassis-poweron",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Zoey YJ Chung",
                        "email": "zoey.yj.chung.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "zoeychung10"
                    },
                    "message": "May I kindly confirm the different power control flows\u2014 is this your intended meaning? Thanks.\n\nFor AC on case:\nAC on service \u2192 DC on service\n(No need to run phosphor-discover-system-state)\n\nFor Sled cycle case:\nAC on service \u2192 DC on service\n(No need to run phosphor-discover-system-state)\n\nFor BMC reboot case:\nAC on service \u2192 phosphor-discover-system-state \u2192 DC on or DC off service (depending on alwaysOn / alwaysOff policy)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-yosemite4/recipes-phosphor/state/phosphor-state-manager/policy-chassis-poweron",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Zoey YJ Chung",
                        "email": "zoey.yj.chung.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "zoeychung10"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @patrick@stwcx.xyz,\nThanks for the reminder.I will update this to support different policy scenarios. \n\nMay I kindly confirm in which power control flows the Power Policy is actually applied? Is it only during BMC reboot? (Currently, the policy is checked during AC ON, AC cycle, Sled cycle, and BMC reboot.) Thanks!"
                }
            ],
